<title>BULGARIA: Bulgaria cancels T-bill issue, cites rate rise.</title>
<headline>Bulgaria cancels T-bill issue, cites rate rise.</headline>
<dateline>SOFIA 1996-09-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bulgaria's Finance Ministry cancelled Monday's auction of 49-day discount T-bills because of the change in the central interest rate (CIR), the central bank (BNB) said.</p>
<p>On Monday the BNB hiked the CIR to a record high 300 percent from 108 percent, effective Tuesday, in a bid to restore confidence in the falling lev.</p>
<p>Details of the cancelled issue follow:</p>
<p> Issue number		BG 3018796006</p>
<p> Type			  Discount</p>
<p> Par value		   5.2 bln levs</p>
<p> Auction date		Sept 23, 1996</p>
<p> Issue date		  Sept 25, 1996</p>
<p> Maturity date	     Nov 13, 1996</p>
<p>-- Sofia Newsroom, (++359-2) 981 8569</p>
